## Explanation

A user wants to access `www.foobar.com`.

The DNS resolves the domain name to the infrastructure.

The request reaches a load balancer cluster made of two HAProxy load balancers.

The load balancers are configured as a cluster to avoid having a single load balancer as a Single Point of Failure.

The request is then forwarded to the web server.

The web server, Nginx, handles HTTP or HTTPS requests and serves static content.

For dynamic content, the web server forwards the request to the application server.

The application server runs the backend code and business logic.

If data is needed, the application server communicates with the database server.

The database server runs MySQL and stores the website data.

## Why We Added Each Element

### Additional Server

The additional server allows us to separate the infrastructure components.

Instead of putting the web server, application server, and database on the same machine, each component can have its own server.

This improves scalability, performance, and maintainability.

### Second Load Balancer

The second load balancer is added to create a load balancer cluster.

This removes the load balancer as a Single Point of Failure.

If one load balancer fails, the other one can continue receiving traffic.

### Load Balancer Cluster

The HAProxy load balancers are configured as a cluster.

This improves availability and reliability.

The cluster can work in Active-Passive mode or Active-Active mode.

### Separated Web Server

The web server is separated so it can focus on handling HTTP requests and serving static files.

### Separated Application Server

The application server is separated so it can focus on running the backend logic.

### Separated Database Server

The database server is separated so it can focus on storing and retrieving data efficiently.

## Benefits of This Infrastructure

This infrastructure is easier to scale.

Each layer can be improved independently:
- More web servers can be added
- More application servers can be added
- Database replication can be added
- Load balancers can be clustered

It also improves reliability because components are separated and easier to monitor, maintain, and debug.